public int minCostClimbingStairs(int[] cost) {
    int n = cost.length;
    int dp0 = 0, dp1 = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int temp = dp0;
        dp0 = Math.min(dp0, dp1) + cost[i];
        dp1 = temp;
    }
    return Math.min(dp0, dp1);
}
```
This function uses the Dynamic Programming approach, where we maintain two variables `dp0` and `dp1` to keep track of the minimum cost to reach the top of the stairs from either the previous step or two steps ago, respectively. We update these variables at each step and return the minimum of the two at the end.

Time complexity : O(n)
Space complexity : O(1)

